content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line; findings reported at the drive-end housing.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS at the drive-end housing. The applicable manual method is vibration velocity measured on both bearing housings, with the highest reading classified using Figure 3. Figure 3 defines Zone C as 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS, 'Restricted - plan maintenance', and Zone D as 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The reading is exactly on the C/D boundary, and the figure expressly does not establish which zone owns a boundary value. Therefore neither a definitive Zone C nor Zone D classification can be made from this evidence. The non-drive-end reading required for a complete highest-reading classification was not reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using the manual's bearing-housing surface-temperature criterion, 72 C exceeds the documented normal limit of up to 70 C by 2 C. It remains below the 80 C alarm by 8 C and below the 90 C trip by 18 C. Thus the applicable normal limit is exceeded, but the temperature evidence does not show that either the alarm or trip threshold has been reached.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leak is reported. The troubleshooting table invokes mechanical-seal replacement for the symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal'; that symptom alone therefore does not justify scheduling a seal replacement here. No numerical allowable-leakage limit is supplied, and absence of leakage does not resolve the vibration or temperature abnormalities.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — check first because it is a documented probable cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, the two abnormal findings in the report. This is a suspected cause, not a confirmed diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment — effectively a joint-first check with bearing wear because it is also documented as a probable cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — documented for high bearing temperature; check grease quantity before attributing the 72 C reading solely to bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage — documented as a probable cause of high vibration; inspect the impeller as part of troubleshooting.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation — also documented as a probable cause of high vibration; check NPSH. No cavitation reading or NPSH acceptance value is provided in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 now as a conservative precaution and hold it out of service pending resolution of the exact 7.1 mm/s RMS zone boundary. This hold is not a claim that the reading is definitively Zone D: Zone C would require restricted operation and planned maintenance, whereas Zone D would require stopping the pump. Engineering must resolve the boundary before normal operation is resumed or any diagnostic running is authorised.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Preserve the reported drive-end reading and obtain the missing non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration measurement when safe and authorised. Classify the highest of the two readings under Figure 3 and record the weekly measurements; do not treat the single supplied reading as a complete both-housings assessment.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the common causes first: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings for wear, noise or high temperature, and check alignment. Also inspect the impeller for imbalance or damage and check NPSH. Record actual findings and measurements so that the conditional replacement work below can be authorised on evidence rather than assumed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 and non-drive-end HF3-510. For applicable reassembly using Table 5's lightly-oiled-thread values, tighten M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm and, if removed, the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Whenever the casing is opened, fit one new HF3-120 casing gasket. Where casing bolts are disturbed and Table 5 applies, tighten the M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not replace the mechanical seal merely as a response to leakage, because no leak was reported. If diagnosis separately authorises seal replacement, isolate and drain the pump, remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. For this serial-numbered pump, fit HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth, fit a new casing gasket, and tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than the manual's superseded 25 Nm value. Apply the M24 impeller-nut torque of 160 Nm and other applicable Table 5 torques where specified.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment to a parallel offset tolerance of 0.05 mm and angular tolerance of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Following repair, record vibration on both bearing housings and the housing-surface temperature, classify the highest vibration reading, and apply the action for the confirmed zone. Compare temperature again with normal 70 C, alarm 80 C and trip 90 C. Resume the documented weekly vibration-monitoring routine; do not silently treat the unresolved 7.1 boundary as acceptable.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Conditional drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Supply one, but fit only as part of a bearing-pair replacement when either bearing meets the manual's wear, noise or high-temperature criterion.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Conditional non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Supply one and replace together with HF3-512 when bearing-pair replacement is confirmed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; one required whenever the casing is opened, including the manual seal-replacement procedure. Not automatically required if the casing remains closed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Conditional cartridge mechanical seal, one only if seal replacement is separately confirmed. This is the required replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above; do not substitute HF3-450 on P-103. The cartridge is pre-set.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve, one only if inspection during applicable seal work finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the precautionary stop and hold while the vibration-zone boundary is unresolved. The evidence supports this as a conservative response to a possible Zone D condition, not as a definitive classification of the reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-103 falls within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Include this chemical in the pre-job hazard review and obtain the site's handling, PPE and decontamination requirements before draining or opening wetted equipment; those detailed requirements are not in the supplied evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For mechanical-seal replacement, isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge during operation and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement, if inspection confirms it: standard labour is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for replacement of the bearing pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, when required after work moving the motor or bearing housing: standard labour is 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual's standard for mechanical-seal replacement is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. Apply this only as a conditional planning reference for now: the service bulletin changes this asset's seal to cartridge HF3-450B but does not state whether the standard time changes.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No evidenced standard duration is available for the initial vibration, grease, alignment, impeller or NPSH diagnosis. Do not add those inspections to the conditional standard times as though they were included; Table 6 lists only seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict resolved for this asset: the generic parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 says not to fit HF3-450 on pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and to use cartridge HF3-450B instead. P-103 is HF3-22410 and is therefore inside that explicit range, so HF3-450B governs if a seal is replaced. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026; the decision is based on its express serial scope, not on an assumed issue date for manual Revision D, whose date is not supplied. Pumps below HF3-22000 remain on HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict resolved for this asset: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while the applicable bulletin gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Use 30 Nm for HF3-450B on P-103; do not use the generic 25 Nm entry for that cartridge. The bulletin does not revise the other Table 5 fastener torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which zone owns a reading exactly equal to 7.1 mm/s RMS? Figure 3 explicitly leaves boundary ownership unspecified. Obtain the manufacturer's or responsible engineering authority's ruling and the corresponding return-to-service decision; the P1 priority and immediate stop in this work order are conservative planning choices, not a documented site priority definition or a definitive Zone D classification. [C07]",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration reading, and when were both readings last taken? Weekly measurements on both housings and classification of the highest reading are required, but only one drive-end value was reported. [C06]",
    "Was the 72 C temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface using the manual's stated basis, and at which housing? The report says only 'housing temperature'; confirm the location and method before final trending or acceptance. [C01, C02]",
    "What are the grease quantity and specification, actual alignment readings, bearing condition/noise findings, impeller condition, and NPSH result? These determine which conditional tasks and parts are needed. The evidence gives troubleshooting directions but no grease-quantity or NPSH acceptance limits. [C09, C10]",
    "What site-specific isolation verification, sodium-hypochlorite PPE, draining, flushing and decontamination controls apply? The evidence identifies the chemical dosing but does not supply those procedures. [C10, C16]",
    "Does the manual's 4.0-hour, 2-technician seal-replacement standard remain valid for cartridge HF3-450B? The bulletin changes the part, preset method and gland torque but provides no revised labour time. [C12, C13]"
  ]
}
